==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] (4,000%) spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Those Guys]] (100%) spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 6~20 seconds<sup>180f~600f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn, delay 10~30 seconds<sup>300f~900f</sup>.
**3 [[Kory|Kories]] spawn, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
**2 [[Kory|Kories]] spawn, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
**1 [[Kory]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Stack [[:Category:Cats with Wave Immunity|wave immune]] cats by using [[Li'l Tank Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Tank Cat]] to meatshield. Since his range is lower than any enemy's range, the enemies will separate based on range and die one by one to your ranged attackers. It's important to not let your meatshields die, because otherwise a clump of peons will die and you'll lose valuable distance. Thus, plan to have at least 3-4 meatshields alive at all times. If you stack 4 [[Miyamoku Musashi (Special Cat)|Musashis]], you will probably win the stage. [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk]] is also a good cat to stack for the crowd control he offers, although admittedly needing support from [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Blockers]]. Using [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus]] with Cat Production combos along with ranged cats like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris]] is also advised.

If you happen to have [[Brainwashed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Bird Cat]], they will dismantle the stage with their wave immunity and massive damage to Traitless enemies, especially with support from the likes of [[Kung Fu Cat (Special Cat)|Talented Dancer]] and [[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]].

